From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:03:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 12/39] Metal diamond engine: multithreaded operator setup, GPU
 timing diagnostics (snapshot cg24)

Operator_Metal_Diamond now derives from Operator_Multithread instead of
Operator_SSE_Compressed, so Calc_EC (material averaging), CalcPEC, the timestep
search and Calc_ECOperatorPos run on every core, as for the multithreaded engine
(the same operator: the multithreaded engine has always used it). Operator setup on
a loaded M5 before -> after (the multithreaded engine's): notch x3 5.55 -> 2.74 s
(2.61), patch x5 6.48 -> 1.69 s (1.60), SMA launch 1.25 -> 0.57 s (0.59), GCPW line
0.31 -> 0.13 s (0.14), patch tutorial 0.17 -> 0.03 s (0.03).

OPENEMS_DIAMOND_TIMING=1 also prints the IterateTS calls (steps per call), the
command buffers and their GPU time (busy, and first start to last end per call);
=2 commits every phase dispatch in a command buffer of its own and splits the GPU
time by phase (MM, MV, VM, VV). The verbose dims line names the operator count.
The --engine help text lists the extensions the GPU runs.

emsKit diamond_check.sh 54 of 54; all six benchmark models bit-identical to the
multithreaded engine with OPENEMS_FTZ=1 (probes rel 0, S-parameters 0 dB). The CPU
engines are unchanged.

